# G076 — Bookmark Collector and Sorter

*v2. See `bookmarks.md` for prose: folders and tags as orthogonal
first-class axes, URL as natural key, sort as view never storage,
flat path strings for hierarchy, cross-axis search, upsert on re-add.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Research Session Capture

[capture-research @topic
    IN ORDER TO
        record every page visit with topic-derived folder and extracted tags
        upserting by URL so revisiting a page updates rather than duplicates
        and surfacing sorted views without mutating storage order

    @collection <- [bookmarks[new-collection]]

    sync @browse-events {
        visit @page ->
            [bookmarks[add
                        {collection: @collection,
                         url: @page:url,
                         title: @page:title,
                         folder: [classify[folder {topic: @topic}]],
                         tags: [extract[tags {page: @page}]],
                         added-ms: [clock[now]]}]]

        view-by-date ->
            @view <- [bookmarks[sorted
                                  {collection: @collection,
                                   by: "added-ms",
                                   order: "desc"}]]
            [ui[render-list {items: @view}]]

        view-by-tag @tag ->
            @view <- [bookmarks[by-tag
                                  {collection: @collection, tag: @tag}]]
            [ui[render-list {items: @view}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[bookmarks
    new-collection
    add              {collection, url, title, folder, tags, added-ms}
                                                    ;; upsert by url
    remove           {collection, id}
    by-folder        {collection, prefix}            ;; recursive prefix match
    by-tag           {collection, tag}
    search           {collection, needle}            ;; cross-axis
    sorted           {collection, by, order}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: upsert by natural key `where` url matches

[bookmarks[add {collection: @c, url: @u, ...}]
    IN ORDER TO
        treat URL as the natural key so re-adding updates in place
        keeping the id stable while title, folder, tags refresh

    @existing <- @c:entries where url is @u
    @existing
        where exists
            -> update @existing:title, :folder, :tags, :added-ms in place
        otherwise
            -> insert new entry with fresh id at end (insertion order)
]

Natural keys are domain-given (URL, file path, agent name); surrogate
ids exist for reference stability. Choosing identity correctly is
the deepest schema question G076 commits to answering via upsert.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: sort as view, storage stays natural order

[bookmarks[sorted {collection: @c, by: @key, order: @ord}]
    @c:entries
        ordered by @key in direction @ord
        stable (insertion order breaks ties)
    IN ORDER TO
        compute the view on demand without mutating storage
        so multiple callers can request different sorts concurrently
        and add/remove remains O(1)
]

Sort never touches the stored list. Every sort is a lens. Same
discipline G088 picks for file records but made more explicit here:
"storage order is insertion; sorts are derived."

## Distinctive Innate idiom: folder prefix `where` path begins with

[bookmarks[by-folder {collection: @c, prefix: @p}]
    @c:entries
        where folder is equal to @p
        or    folder begins with @p + "/"
]

Hierarchy lives in the string, not in a materialised tree. Same
choice filesystems, URL paths, and CSS selectors make. Don't
materialise structure you don't query.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @c <- [bookmarks[new-collection]]
    [bookmarks[add {collection: @c, url: "https://rust-lang.org",
                     title: "Rust", folder: "/dev/languages",
                     tags: ["programming", "rust"], added-ms: 1000}]]
    [bookmarks[add {collection: @c, url: "https://news.example",
                     title: "News", folder: "/news",
                     tags: ["daily"], added-ms: 2000}]]
    [bookmarks[add {collection: @c, url: "https://rust-lang.org",
                     title: "The Rust Language",
                     folder: "/dev/languages",
                     tags: ["programming", "rust", "systems"],
                     added-ms: 3000}]]
    ;; upsert: id stable, title/tags updated

    -> [bookmarks[by-folder {collection: @c, prefix: "/dev"}]]
    ;; -> [one entry, url rust-lang.org]

    -> [bookmarks[by-tag {collection: @c, tag: "systems"}]]
    ;; -> [one entry]

    -> [bookmarks[sorted
                    {collection: @c,
                     by: "added-ms", order: "desc"}]]
    ;; -> [rust (ms=3000), news (ms=2000)]
]
